EXPERIMENT 41 – SMOKE TESTING ON A MESSAGING APPLICATION
AIM
To execute smoke testing on a new version of a messaging application. Smoke testing is a quick and shallow check of the critical functions of a new build to decide whether it is stable enough for detailed testing.
ALGORITHM
1. Install the new build of the messaging application on the test device.
2. Prepare a checklist covering only the critical functions. Keep it short enough to execute within 15–30 minutes.
3. Execute the checklist in the given order.
4. If any critical function fails, stop testing.
5. If all checks pass, accept the build for detailed testing. Otherwise, reject it and report the failed checks to developers.
6. Record the build number and check the network connection before testing.
7. Record the final decision and stop.
INPUT
Pre-requisites and Test Environment
Item	Details
Build under test	New messaging application build
Devices	One Android and one iOS device
Accounts	Two test accounts
Time limit	30 minutes
Rule	If any critical check fails, reject the build and stop testing

Smoke Test Checklist
TC ID	Critical Function	Test
SM01	Install and launch	Install and open application
SM02	Login	Login using mobile number and OTP
SM03	Send text	Send a text message
SM04	Receive text	Receive a message from another device
SM05	Send image	Send an image from gallery
SM06	Create group	Create group with two members
SM07	Notification	Receive message while app is in background
SM08	Logout	Logout from application
SM09	Delete a message	Delete a sent message
SM10	Upgrade	Install new build over old build

OUTPUT
All 10 test cases passed.
Build Number	Date	Checks Passed	Checks Failed	Decision
Build 2.5.0	10 Nov 2026	10	0	Accepted for detailed testing

RESULT
Thus, smoke testing of the new version of the messaging application was executed. All critical functions passed, and the build was accepted for detailed testing.
